@startuml SmartLost_Authentication_Sequence
title SmartLost - UML Authentication Sequence\nUC02 Sign in, session renewal and UC03 Sign out
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 65

actor "Campus User" as User
boundary "Angular Web App\n[Planned semester work]" as Web #FAF5FF
box "Auth Service API - one application process" #EFF6FF
  boundary "Auth API\nController, mapping and validation pipeline" as API
  control "Auth Command Handlers" as Commands
  participant "UserAccountRepository" as Repository
  participant "PasswordService" as Passwords
  control "AuthenticationSessionService" as Sessions
  participant "TokenService" as Tokens
end box
database "Auth Database\nPostgreSQL" as DB

note over API, DB
  Existing backend: register, login and refresh.
  Database operations use EF Core / AuthDbContext.
  Purple messages describe planned semester additions.
end note

== UC02 - Sign in ==
User -> Web : Enter email and password
Web -> API : POST /api/auth/login\n{ email, password }
API -> API : Map request to LoginUserCommand\nValidate email and password
alt Invalid command
  API --> Web : 400 Bad Request / ProblemDetails
  Web --> User : Display validation errors
else Valid command
  API -> Commands : Handle LoginUserCommand
  Commands -> Repository : FindByEmailAsync(normalizedEmail)\nTrim + ToUpperInvariant
  Repository -> DB : Find user by normalized email
  DB --> Repository : UserAccount or no account
  Repository --> Commands : UserAccount or null
  opt Account exists
    Commands -> Passwords : Verify(userAccount, password)
    Passwords --> Commands : Password verification result
  end
  alt Unknown email or incorrect password
    Commands --> API : Unauthorized result\nauth.invalid_credentials
    API --> Web : 401 Unauthorized / ProblemDetails\nSame credentials error in both cases
    Web --> User : Display sign-in error
  else Valid credentials
    Commands -> Sessions : CreateAsync(userAccount)
    Sessions -> Sessions : Generate cryptographically random refresh token\nCompute SHA-256 hash and absolute session expiry
    Sessions -> Tokens : CreateToken(userAccount)
    Tokens --> Sessions : Signed JWT and access-token expiry
    Sessions -> Repository : SaveChangesAsync()\nCommit tracked session and token history
    Repository -> DB : Insert RefreshSession and RefreshToken\nPersist refresh-token hashes only
    DB --> Repository : Committed
    Repository --> Sessions : Saved
    Sessions --> Commands : AuthResponse
    Commands --> API : Success result
    API --> Web : 200 OK / AuthResponse\nUser details, access token, refresh token and expiries
    Web --> User : Display authenticated application
  end
end

== Session renewal - separate request after successful sign in ==
note over Web, API
  A refresh request does not require a valid access token.
  This interaction supports FR03; it is not a separate user goal.
end note
Web -> API : POST /api/auth/refresh\n{ refreshToken }
API -> API : Map RefreshTokenCommand and validate token format
alt Invalid token format
  API --> Web : 400 Bad Request / ProblemDetails
else Valid format
  API -> Commands : Handle RefreshTokenCommand
  Commands -> Sessions : RefreshAsync(refreshToken)
  Sessions -> Sessions : Compute SHA-256 hash
  Sessions -> DB : Find token history with session and user\nvia AuthDbContext
  DB --> Sessions : Stored token, session and user, or no match
  alt Unknown token, expired session or revoked session
    Sessions --> Commands : Unauthorized result\nauth.invalid_refresh_token
  else Previously used token in an active session
    Sessions -> DB : Revoke that refresh session
    DB --> Sessions : Revocation persisted
    Sessions --> Commands : Unauthorized result\nauth.invalid_refresh_token
  else Current token in an active session
    Sessions -> Sessions : Generate replacement refresh token and hash\nKeep the original absolute session expiry
    Sessions -> Tokens : CreateToken(user)
    Tokens --> Sessions : New JWT and access-token expiry
    Sessions -> DB : Atomically update current token hash and insert history\nCheck current hash and revocation concurrency tokens
    alt Rotation committed
      DB --> Sessions : Saved
      Sessions --> Commands : Success with new AuthResponse
    else Concurrent refresh or revocation detected
      DB --> Sessions : DbUpdateConcurrencyException
      Sessions -> DB : Revoke that refresh session
      DB --> Sessions : Revocation persisted or already revoked
      Sessions --> Commands : Unauthorized result\nauth.invalid_refresh_token
    end
  end
  Commands --> API : Result<AuthResponse>
  API --> Web : 200 OK with replacement tokens\nor 401 Unauthorized / ProblemDetails
  Web -> Web : On success, replace the previous token pair
end

== UC03 - Sign out [Planned semester work] ==
note over Web, Sessions #FAF5FF
  Target behaviour from FR03 / UC03, not an existing endpoint.
  The route and detailed revocation contract are not defined yet.
end note
User -[#7E22CE]> Web : Select Sign out
Web -[#7E22CE]> API : Request revocation of the current refresh session
API -[#7E22CE]> Commands : Dispatch planned sign-out command\nValidate the caller's authority over the session
Commands -[#7E22CE]> Sessions : Request current-session revocation
Sessions -[#7E22CE]> DB : Persist revocation for that session only
DB -[#7E22CE]-> Sessions : Revocation outcome
Sessions -[#7E22CE]-> Commands : Outcome
Commands -[#7E22CE]-> API : Result
API -[#7E22CE]-> Web : Confirm revocation or report failure
Web -[#7E22CE]> Web : Clear browser credentials even on request failure
Web -[#7E22CE]-> User : Return to sign-in view\nReport if server revocation was not confirmed
note over Web, DB
  Sign out must be safe to repeat and must not revoke other sessions.
  Already issued JWTs remain valid until expiry unless extra revocation is added.
end note
@enduml
